<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Unidare says welding executive resigns.</title>
<headline>Unidare says welding executive resigns.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unidare Plc said on Monday that John Garland, responsible for its British, Irish and Dutch welding activities, had resigned to take up another position outside the welding industry.</p>
<p>Garland, who resigns with effect from December 1, will continue as a non-executive director of Unidare, the engineering group said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
